FEX: HideHypervisorBit also hides the hypervisor CPUID leaves (Darwin host)

HideHypervisorBit only cleared CPUID.1:ECX[31]; leaves 4000_0000h
("FEXIFEXIEMU") and 4000_0001h (host architecture = AArch64) stayed. The
Steam client reads them: under SteamARM it concluded it ran on an arm64
host and installed Proton (ARM64), Steam Linux Runtime 4.0 - Arm64 and
Steam's own FEX tool (MEASURED), a path that cannot work on macOS -- native
aarch64 Wine would need the low 4 GiB, which Darwin's __PAGEZERO takes. With
the option set, both leaves read as zero and the machine looks like x86-64
Linux: Steam uses x86 Proton, which runs under this FEX's low window.

